Feature: Supplier Risk Analyst Risk Assessment and Monitoring
  As Priya Patel, Supplier Risk Analyst
  I want to transform supplier risk management from manual to automated processes
  So that I can provide predictive risk intelligence and early warning capabilities for supply chain protection

  Background:
    Given I am logged in as Priya Patel, Supplier Risk Analyst
    And I have access to the supplier risk intelligence system
    And I am responsible for continuous monitoring and assessment of supplier risks
    And I work with various data sources and analytical tools

  @automated-monitoring @real-time-alerts
  Scenario: Automated supplier risk monitoring with real-time alerts
    Given I need to monitor thousands of suppliers continuously
    And manual monitoring is not scalable or timely
    When the automated risk monitoring system detects significant risk changes
    Then I should receive real-time alerts for suppliers exceeding risk thresholds
    And alerts should include specific risk factors and severity levels
    And I should be able to configure alert thresholds by risk category
    And I should have access to supporting data and analysis behind each alert
    And I should be able to escalate critical alerts to appropriate stakeholders

  @data-integration @automated-collection
  Scenario: Automated data collection from multiple risk data sources
    Given I currently spend 70% of my time manually collecting data
    And risk data comes from disparate sources including financial, regulatory, and news
    When I configure automated data integration
    Then the system should automatically collect data from:
      | Data Source Type        | Examples                                          |
      | Financial databases     | D&B, Bloomberg, supplier financial statements    |
      | Regulatory databases    | FDA, EPA, customs and trade databases           |
      | News and media         | Reuters, Bloomberg News, industry publications   |
      | Government databases   | SEC filings, patent databases, regulatory actions|
      | Supplier self-reported | Supplier portals, questionnaires, certifications|
    And data should be normalized and validated automatically
    And I should focus on analysis rather than data collection

  @predictive-modeling @risk-forecasting
  Scenario: Develop predictive models for proactive risk management
    Given historical risk patterns can help predict future supplier issues
    When I develop and deploy predictive risk models
    Then I should be able to use machine learning algorithms for risk prediction
    And models should incorporate multiple risk indicators and their correlations
    And I should achieve >90% accuracy in predicting high-risk suppliers
    And I should provide early warning alerts 30-60 days before issues materialize
    And I should continuously improve model performance with new data

  @tariff-impact-analysis @trade-policy
  Scenario: Analyze tariff impact on supplier portfolio in real-time
    Given new tariffs are announced on imports from specific countries
    And I need to quickly assess impact across our supplier portfolio
    When I run tariff impact analysis
    Then I should see immediate impact assessment for all affected suppliers
    And I should see financial impact calculations by supplier and category
    And I should identify suppliers most vulnerable to tariff changes
    And I should provide ranking of suppliers by tariff exposure severity
    And I should generate recommendations for risk mitigation strategies

  @risk-scoring @methodology-development
  Scenario: Configure and maintain supplier risk scoring algorithms
    Given different risk factors have varying importance for different supplier types
    When I configure risk scoring methodologies
    Then I should be able to customize risk scoring weights by category:
      | Risk Factor           | Electronics | Apparel | Food & Beverage |
      | Financial stability   | 25%        | 30%     | 35%            |
      | Geographic location   | 30%        | 25%     | 15%            |
      | Regulatory compliance | 20%        | 20%     | 35%            |
      | Operational capacity  | 15%        | 15%     | 10%            |
      | ESG factors          | 10%        | 10%     | 5%             |
    And I should be able to adjust scoring algorithms based on business priorities
    And I should test and validate scoring accuracy against known outcomes

  @portfolio-analysis @trend-identification
  Scenario: Analyze risk trends across entire supplier portfolio
    Given I need to identify systemic risks and emerging trends
    When I conduct portfolio-wide risk analysis
    Then I should see risk distribution patterns across geographic regions
    And I should identify correlation patterns between different risk factors
    And I should detect emerging risk trends before they become critical
    And I should benchmark our portfolio risk against industry standards
    And I should provide strategic recommendations for portfolio optimization

  @deep-dive-analysis @supplier-investigation
  Scenario: Conduct detailed risk assessment for critical suppliers
    Given a supplier is flagged for potential risk issues
    And the supplier represents significant business value or risk
    When I conduct a deep-dive risk assessment
    Then I should have access to comprehensive supplier intelligence including:
      | Assessment Area        | Analysis Components                              |
      | Financial health       | Financial ratios, cash flow, debt analysis     |
      | Operational risks      | Capacity utilization, technology, workforce    |
      | Regulatory compliance  | Certifications, violations, legal issues       |
      | Geographic risks       | Political stability, natural disasters, infrastructure |
      | Market position        | Competitive strength, customer concentration    |
    And I should provide actionable recommendations with confidence levels
    And I should document analysis methodology and supporting evidence

  @scenario-modeling @stress-testing
  Scenario: Model risk scenarios and conduct supplier portfolio stress testing
    Given I need to understand portfolio vulnerability under different scenarios
    When I conduct scenario modeling and stress testing
    Then I should be able to model various risk scenarios including:
      | Scenario Type          | Examples                                        |
      | Trade policy changes   | New tariffs, trade war escalation             |
      | Natural disasters      | Earthquakes, floods, hurricanes in key regions |
      | Economic disruption    | Recession, currency devaluation, inflation    |
      | Regulatory changes     | New safety standards, environmental regulations |
      | Geopolitical events    | Political instability, sanctions, conflicts   |
    And I should see impact projections for each scenario
    And I should identify most vulnerable suppliers under each scenario
    And I should provide mitigation recommendations for high-risk scenarios

  @stakeholder-reporting @communication
  Scenario: Generate risk reports and insights for procurement stakeholders
    Given different stakeholders need different levels of risk information
    When I create risk reports and communications
    Then I should be able to generate customized reports for:
      | Audience               | Report Focus                                    |
      | Executive leadership   | Portfolio-level risks, strategic implications  |
      | Category managers      | Category-specific risks, supplier alternatives |
      | Procurement teams      | Operational risks, supplier recommendations    |
      | Finance teams         | Cost impacts, financial risk exposure         |
      | Operations teams      | Supply continuity, disruption probabilities   |
    And reports should be actionable with clear recommendations
    And I should be able to schedule automated report distribution

  @continuous-learning @model-improvement
  Scenario: Continuously improve risk models based on outcomes and feedback
    Given risk models need continuous refinement to maintain accuracy
    When I evaluate model performance and incorporate feedback
    Then I should track model prediction accuracy against actual outcomes
    And I should identify factors that improve or reduce model performance
    And I should incorporate new risk indicators and data sources
    And I should validate model improvements through backtesting
    And I should maintain model documentation and change history

  @integration @workflow-optimization
  Scenario: Integrate risk intelligence with procurement decision workflows
    Given risk insights need to be actionable within procurement processes
    When procurement teams make supplier-related decisions
    Then risk scores should be automatically available in procurement systems
    And risk alerts should trigger appropriate approval workflows
    And I should provide risk consulting support for complex decisions
    And I should track how risk intelligence influences procurement decisions
    And I should measure business value generated by risk intelligence

  @professional-development @analytical-capabilities
  Scenario: Enhance analytical capabilities and stay current with best practices
    Given risk management is a rapidly evolving field
    When I work on professional development and capability building
    Then I should have access to advanced analytical tools and techniques
    And I should participate in industry risk management communities
    And I should stay current with emerging risk factors and methodologies
    And I should contribute to MegaMart's risk management thought leadership
    And I should mentor junior analysts and share knowledge across the organization
